Description:
CREATE TABLE t0(c0 LONGTEXT) ;
INSERT INTO t0(c0) VALUES(0.1);
CREATE TABLE t1(c0 INT ZEROFILL PRIMARY KEY) ;
INSERT IGNORE INTO t1(c0) VALUES(NULL);

SELECT !((LEAST(t0.c0, t1.c0)) || (t1.c0)) FROM t1, t0; -- {0}
SELECT * FROM t1, t0 WHERE !((LEAST(t0.c0, t1.c0)) || (t1.c0)); -- {0000000000, 0.1}

In the first query, the expression !((LEAST(t0.c0, t1.c0)) is evaluated to false, while the second query still returns non-empty result.

How to repeat:
docker run -it -p 3306:3306 -e MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD=root mysql:8.2.0

Then execute the above test case.
